# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
#   Windows:  copy .env.example .env
# .env is gitignored - it is never committed. Never paste a real key into
# .env.example itself.

# --- Groq (free-tier API) --------------------------------------------------
# Required only if you set GROUNDTRUTH_GENERATION_PROVIDER=groq below, or pass
# --config for a config file with generation.provider: groq.
# Get a key at https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- Generation provider switch ---------------------------------------------
# Optional. Every checked-in config (configs/*.yaml) has generation.provider: ollama
# on disk - that stays the default and is never edited by this switch. Setting these
# here overrides it at runtime for every command (ask/run), without touching any
# config file, so you can flip between Ollama and Groq per environment.
#
# Leave both blank/commented to keep using Ollama (the on-disk default).
#
# GROUNDTRUTH_GENERATION_PROVIDER=groq
# GROUNDTRUTH_GENERATION_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.8-27b
#
# Groq's free-tier model catalog changes over time and older model names get
# retired - check https://console.groq.com/docs/models for what's current, or
# list what YOUR key can actually see:
#   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $GROQ_API_KEY" https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/models
#
# Verified against a real free-tier key on 2026-09-28 (chat-capable models only -
# that endpoint also lists Whisper/audio and Prompt-Guard/classifier models, which
# this project does not use):
#   qwen/qwen3.8-27b      - recommended default: fastest of the three, correctly
#                           follows the "[1]"-style citation instruction, clean
#                           ASCII output. (If GROUNDTRUTH_GENERATION_MODEL is left
#                           unset, switching provider to groq falls back to this
#                           automatically - see config.py:_PROVIDER_DEFAULT_MODELS.)
#   openai/gpt-oss-20b    - also solid; used a typographic hyphen (‑) instead of a
#                           plain "-" in one test, cosmetic only
#   openai/gpt-oss-120b   - higher capacity, but cited with fullwidth brackets
#                           (【1】) instead of "[1]" in testing - would need the
#                           prompt or a citation regex adjusted to rely on it
